jit: let a thread spinning in a conditional loop be suspended

Another thread suspends an emulated one cooperatively: Wine sets the thread's suspend doorbell
and FEX's generated code looks at it, stopping at a brk #0xCAFE with its state saved. The code
looks at the start of each block and before unconditional jumps back, but not before
conditional ones. A spin loop like "while (!flag) count++;" ends in a conditional jump back, so
a thread in one never saw the doorbell, and SuspendThread + GetThreadContext on it waited
forever. Garbage collectors stop every thread this way. Genshin Impact froze on its warning
screen: one thread spun at 100% in emulated code while another waited in NtGetContextThread
for it, with no disk reads.

The check now also goes before a conditional jump back to guest code, meaning a block that is an
entry point or sits at a nonzero guest offset. A guest jcc has computed its flags and flushed the
register cache already, so the state can be reconstructed there, and the check (ldr + cbz)
leaves NZCV alone. Loops the translator makes inside one guest instruction (rep string ops) jump
to neither and are unchanged. tests/runtime/suspend-spin.c checks loops on the zero and carry
flags.

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
index ae3ed51..4814f9e 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
@@ -250,6 +250,20 @@ DEF_OP(CondJump) {
 
   auto TrueTargetLabel = JumpTarget(Op->TrueBlock);
 
+  // A conditional jump back to a guest instruction is a guest loop, such as a spin loop waiting
+  // for a flag. Without a check here such a loop never sees a suspend request, so another
+  // thread's SuspendThread + GetThreadContext on it waits forever (a garbage collector stopping
+  // every thread). The flags are already computed and the register cache flushed before a guest
+  // jcc, so the state can be reconstructed here, and the check leaves NZCV alone. Blocks of guest
+  // code are entry points or sit at a nonzero guest offset; loops the translator makes inside one
+  // guest instruction (rep string ops) jump to neither and keep running as before.
+  if (TrueTargetLabel->Backward.Location) {
+    const auto TrueBlock = IR->GetOp<IR::IROp_CodeBlock>(Op->TrueBlock);
+    if (TrueBlock->EntryPoint || TrueBlock->GuestEntryOffset != 0) {
+      EmitSuspendInterruptCheck();
+    }
+  }
+
   if (Op->FromNZCV) {
     b_OrRestart(MapCC(Op->Cond), TrueTargetLabel);
   } else {
